{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg3nJcYz3S6TP2osEreby","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Use the `@variant` directive with the breakpoint name inside your custom CSS (the docs show it with `dark`, but any variant works):\n\n```css\n:root {\n  --my-var: 1rem;\n  @variant md {\n    --my-var: 2rem;\n  }\n}\n```\n\n- `@variant` applies a Tailwind variant to custom CSS: `docs/adding-custom-styles.mdx`, \"Using variants\", and `docs/functions-and-directives.mdx`, \"@variant\". Their examples only use `dark` and `hover`, so using `md` here is my inference.\n- `md` expands to `@media (width >= 48rem)`, and `max-md` to `@media (width < 48rem)`. See the breakpoint tables in `docs/responsive-design.mdx`.\n- In a Vue/Svelte `<style>` block or a CSS module, add `@reference` first (`functions-and-directives.mdx`, \"@reference\")."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5286,"cache_read_input_tokens":17846,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5286},"output_tokens":308,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f24a8e7d-31dc-438c-a592-399c0155b037","uuid":"8891db15-47e3-4c49-8e52-59571644a290","timestamp":"2026-10-15T09:25:12.927Z","request_id":"req_011Cg3nJcENfF6LRZuBrvsFB"}
